* ============================================================================
* workspace_minidb.dts -- a whole database inside one memo field (AIF-070's
* chartered destination, LANDED 2026-08-11 on owner's "do it"). WORKSPACE
* SAVE <name> MEMO MINIDB writes a MINIDB 1 container: the self-locating v3
* posture PLUS every open table's bytes and every attached native index's
* bytes, length-prefixed (binary-safe -- the memo store is payload-agnostic,
* runtime-proven by the zoo on embedded NULs). WORKSPACE LOAD <name> MEMO RAM
* detects the container and hydrates FROM THE PAYLOAD: table bytes flow
* memo -> RAM VFS with ZERO disk reads, then the carried posture stands the
* areas up re-pointed at RAM. Reads are residence-aware (a RAM-resident
* source is read from ramfs), so a RAM session can save its working set
* whole. Plain WORKSPACE LOAD <name> MEMO refuses a MINIDB payload with the
* hydration instruction rather than half-loading.
*
* RUNTIME-PROVEN 2026-08-11 (build 18:35:35, FIRST TRY): mcc_db saved at
* 94200 B (92139 B of table+index bytes + 1443 B posture), oracle
* byte-compare OK on the whole container; hydrated onto a CLEAN RAM disk in
* 65.5 ms -- faster than the disk-sourced hydration (71-94 ms), memory to
* memory; STUDENTS read (200 recs), ENROLL's CDX attached from memo-carried
* bytes via the native fallback; unmount dropped everything, leaving the
* memo as the database's only running-copy source.
*
* Run: DO workspace_minidb | regression: REGRESSION RUN WORKSPACE_MINIDB
* Markers: DB_T1 (row readable from memo-carried table), DB_T2 (order
* attached from memo-carried index).
* ============================================================================
SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF

FORMULA "WS-MINIDB-PROOF-BEGIN"

* --- author the container from the disk-resident MCC ------------------------
DO x64
WORKSPACE CLOSE
WORKSPACE LOAD mcc_x64
WORKSPACE SAVE minidb_regress MEMO MINIDB
WORKSPACE CLOSE

* --- clean RAM disk: the memo is the ONLY source ----------------------------
DO mem
WORKSPACE LOAD minidb_regress MEMO RAM

* --- the database came out of the memo --------------------------------------
VDISK STATUS
SELECT 8
TOP
? "DB_T1_students_from_memo:" + (LNAME > "")
SELECT 4
SET ORDER TAG SID
? "DB_T2_index_from_memo:" + (SID >= 1)

FORMULA "WS-MINIDB-PROOF-END"

* --- teardown ----------------------------------------------------------------
WORKSPACE CLOSE
VDISK UNMOUNT
DO x64
